# Namleh Plugin Cutover

Use this when a tested workflow should graduate from the gstack test fork into
the production Namleh Codex plugin stack.

## Stages

1. Test fork only: `Namleh-Studios/gstack`, generated `namleh-gstack-*` skills.
2. Local repo test: `AGENTS.md` routes in the target repo.
3. Production plugin: `namleh-codex` marketplace package with version bump.
4. Ops Platform integration: workflows become first-party product features or
   hosted MCP capabilities.

## Cutover Checklist

- Skill has been used on real work at least once.
- Trigger is clear and not too broad.
- No gstack-private paths leak into Namleh production.
- Vault rule is preserved.
- Normal repo branch/PR rules are preserved.
- Tests or validation commands exist.
- Tim handoff impact is documented when relevant.
- Rollback path is a plugin version rollback or removal from host include list.

